 through final verification and restarts.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-c639db7b78ff49fe","cmd-4387c6618a36419f"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 before and after execution. The solution uses installed RHEL systemd and Python components, and final package-health checks passed.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","cmd-c639db7b78ff49fe","cmd-4387c6618a36419f"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The initial service definition using nobody was a functional deployment step that also established persistent enablement, then was promptly hardened by replacing it with DynamicUser; the superseded configuration did not remain. The firewall change was directly related to making port 9097 available only to node2. Temporary concurrent-test files and processes were bounded, used for direct verification, and cleaned. Both required node restarts were evidenced, no failed services or package damage remained, and final checks found no test residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-70c0332ae2c8452c","cmd-acdc7690174346a5","cmd-8360ad0eb0484adc","cmd-e6f97e44923a49d9","cmd-f9223eaee35f4706","cmd-c73d348f356047a6","cmd-bd6f858e5f0b4139","cmd-c639db7b78ff49fe","cmd-4387c6618a36419f","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The independent restart protocol is also complete for both managed nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, acknowledged restart, distinct post-restart identity corroborated by fixed lifecycle snapshots, and recovered services, files, networking, and protocol behavior.","limitations":["The implementation uses systemd-socket-activate in its explicit --inetd mode rather than a separately packaged traditional inetd or xinetd daemon; evidence directly establishes the requested inetd-style per-connection behavior.","The first concurrent child-count probe occurred after those clients had already completed and therefore observed zero children, but a subsequent controlled partial-request test directly observed all 12 expected live handler processes and later verified complete cleanup."]}
